{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>He shall send him out.</b> From the root שלוח, like ושלחה מביתו. And the reason it did not write here חנם as above in the case of one who goes out by six years — to teach you that he must give him a document of dismissal, as to his wife." "<b>In place of his tooth.</b> Even though his body is acquired by him, HaShem does not desire that he destroy him in his limbs. The language proves, for with one alone he is free; but if he destroyed his eye and afterward knocked out his tooth, he always receives compensation for the second limb. That a Canaanite slave goes free by the primary limbs is an a fortiori argument: if by Heaven he acquires himself through suffering, as it is written יסור יסרני יה ולמות לא נתנני, then by human agency all the more so."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:35.186622569Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}